# Frontend components

## Structure

- Put reusable UI in `apps/ui/src/components/oriana/`.
- Keep route files in `apps/cms/src/app/(frontend)/` thin: fetch data, compose sections.
- Reuse `PageHero`, `Breadcrumbs`, `FadeIn`, `SiteHeader`, `SiteFooter` before inventing new shells.

## Styling

- Tailwind v4 + tokens from `apps/cms/src/app/(frontend)/globals.css` `@theme`.
- Prefer semantic classes: `text-oriana-navy`, `bg-oriana-surface`, `font-display`, `container`.
- Avoid arbitrary one-off hex except rare gradients already used in heroes.
- Use `cn()` from `@/utilities/ui` for conditional classes.

## Interaction

- Client components only when needed (`'use client'` for motion, menus, forms).
- Follow `vercel-composition-patterns` for compound/flexible APIs; avoid boolean-prop soup.
- For page transitions / shared-element motion, consult `vercel-react-view-transitions`.

## Quality gates

- Keyboard focus visible; interactive elements are real buttons/links.
- Images: Next `Image` or existing `ProductImage`; always meaningful `alt`.
- After larger UI changes, apply `core-web-vitals` / `performance` skills (LCP, CLS, INP).
